cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAG World: a registry and maturity map of retrieval-augmented generation technologies"
message: >-
  If you use this registry or its data, please cite it. Cite a dated release
  rather than the live files: the live files change every week.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Laputski
    given-names: Alexander
repository-code: "https://github.com/laputski/rag-world"
url: "https://ragworld.org"
abstract: >-
  A self-updating registry of retrieval-augmented generation technologies. Every
  record carries a configuration over a stratified schema of twenty-eight
  dimensions across seven strata, a maturity level from L0 to L6 derived by a
  deterministic rule from collected evidence, and the evidence that level rests
  on. Mechanisms the schema cannot express are recorded as residuals, and a
  mechanism seen in three or more records becomes a candidate dimension.
  Evidence is collected weekly from arXiv, OpenAlex, GitHub, PyPI, Papers with
  Code and curated topic lists. No language model takes part in deriving a
  level.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - information retrieval
  - technology readiness
  - configuration space
  - feature model
  - open data
# The object cited here is the registry, that is, the data. It is CC BY 4.0;
# the code that builds it is Apache-2.0 and is cited through the repository.
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://github.com/laputski/rag-world/blob/main/data/LICENSE.md"
